That's not going to be valid, since some of the overdispersion is due to 
the random effect.  Unless the model has fixed effects for site, of 
course, but you haven't said what the model was.

> here is the call:
> 
> glmmPQL(count~ type*collection + offset(log(mass)),
> random=~collection|site, family=negative.binomial(theta=1.17))

How do you manage to have site nested within collection?  Were the trees
moved from site to site?  You haven't explained your design, but that
seems unlikely.  In any case, the advice is to seek statistical
consultancy since teasing out your intentions is an interactive process.

